As per section 3-G (7) of the N.H. Act 1956, the Competent Authority or the Arbitrator while determining the amount under sub-section (1) or sub-section (5),
as the case may he shall take into consideration :-
a) The market value of the land on the date of publication of the notification under section 3-A;
b) The damage, if any, sustained by the person interested at the time of taking possession of the land, by reason of the severing of such land from other land;
c) The damage, if any, sustained by the person interested at the time of taking possession of the land, by reason of the acquisition injuriously affecting their other immovable property in any manner, or their earnings;
Brahmashree Narayana Guru Seva Sangha ... vs The Project Director on 5 February, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/136365054/
